# STOPPING-POINT PROGRAM #3: git pre-commit --changed, the biome-style
# recent-change-lines gating, spelled as ordinary rules. "Which files are NEW
# since a base revision" is a join between two rev-pinned `files_at` host
# answers with `not/1` over the base side; three finding classes ride it
# (banned pattern in a new file, missing required header, whole-tree ratchet
# above a committed ceiling) and land in v5's own 9-column diag_v5 schema.
#
# The receipt drives a REAL four-commit git repository through the served
# engine: c0 baseline, c1 adds one offending file AND one clean control file,
# c2 deletes the offender, c3 advances the base. Every assertion is sorted
# row-set equality, so a rail that fired on every new file would fail on the
# control rather than pass on a count. The ratchet's ceiling is proven data-
# driven by lowering it under an unchanged tree.
#
# The program and its receipt landed at 321a3d4c and were never wired into a
# battery; this recipe is that wiring.
# (expect: GIT-FACT DIAGS RAIL HOLDS, exit 0; ~20s, one ephemeral server)
precommit-changed:
    bash {{ v6 }}/tsv2/scripts/v5-git-diags.sh

# STOPPING-POINT PROGRAM #8 at scale: the watch bind's own cost and correctness
# curve. Duplicate path notifications, edits, identical re-saves and deletes are
# pushed through the real WatchBindRunner and coalesced by a virtual window; the
# final `watch` and `seen` relations are pinned by sha256, and any cell that
# decodes a duplicate, stale or missing row exits 1.
#
# Cost is REPORTED, not gated (wall ms and RSS are machine-dependent); the
# gated part is correctness at each size. A gated cost floor for this path --
# the scale-floor.sh treatment -- does not exist yet and is a named gap in
# v6/READINESS.md.
# (expect: two JSONL lines, correct:true, ticks flat at 3 across both sizes)
# budget: measured 0.7s at 100/1000 files, default 900s -- loose because the
# file counts are arguments and a bigger run is the point (WATCH_SCALE_BUDGET_S)
watch-scale:
    cd {{ v6 }}/tsv2 && {{ capped }} "${WATCH_SCALE_BUDGET_S:-900}" env NODE_NO_WARNINGS=1 \
      node --experimental-transform-types \
      scripts/5_file-watch-scale.ts --files 100,1000 --events-per-file 3 \
      --edit-ratio 0.25 --delete-ratio 0.10 --identical-resave-ratio 0.25

# the v5 surface inventory: every built-in rel, operator and function v5's
# examples/*.dl corpus actually uses, ranked by how many files name it, each
# marked covered / partial / absent against v6. Regenerates
# plans/2026-07-30-v5-parity-table.tsv, so it MUTATES A TRACKED FILE and is
# deliberately outside every battery -- run it when you want the number, and
# commit the table only when the movement is the point.
# (expect: V5 PARITY TABLE SEEDED, exit 0)
v5-parity:
    bash {{ v6 }}/tsv2/scripts/v5-parity.sh

# checked-in gen_emitted modules with no fixture row (door-handwritten.ts)
